  "instructions": {
    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "42000000000000000000000000000001",
        "content": [
          "## PURPOSE\n- Answer claim-level operational questions for adjusters and claims-history users using current claims, adjudications, persisted decision records, manufacturing context, advisory risk, and prior-claim precedent.\n\n## DATA QUALITY NOTES\n- adjudication_decision_records can be empty until decision records have reached the gold layer; disclose that state instead of inferring a trail or citations.\n- customer_heat_risk is advisory context only and never determines verdict, disposition, or approved amount.\n\n## CONSTRAINTS\n- Treat adjudications_current rows with decision_status FINAL as decisions of record; distinguish recommended_verdict from verdict.\n- Use persisted rationale, citations, override_reason, and precedent only; never fabricate policy evidence or recompute settlement amounts.\n- Do not expose customer email, embeddings, hashes, trace identifiers, or hidden raw payloads.\n\n## Instructions you must follow when providing summaries\n- State the claim_id and decision_status for per-claim answers.\n- Label risk and precedent as advisory context, not deterministic authority."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "join_specs": [
      {
        "id": "43000000000000000000000000000001",
        "left": {
          "identifier": "fe-bar-ir.gold.claims_current",
          "alias": "claims_current"
        },
        "right": {
          "identifier": "fe-bar-ir.gold.adjudications_current",
          "alias": "adjudications_current"
        },
        "sql": [
          "`claims_current`.`claim_id` = `adjudications_current`.`claim_id`",
          "--rt=FROM_RELATIONSHIP_TYPE_ONE_TO_ONE--"
